Subject: [PATCH] tun: add default-interface-priority config and reset stale sessions on switch

Problem:
1. Mihomo's tun configuration has no declarative primary/backup interface
   priority list, leaving multi-homed Windows hosts exposed to sing-tun
   metric oscillation between Wi-Fi and wired adapters.
2. When sing-tun's DefaultInterfaceMonitor switches to another default
   interface after the active adapter disconnects, server.go only calls
   iface.FlushCache() and resolver.ResetConnection(). Existing TCP/UDP
   flows in statistic.DefaultManager and pooled anytls client sessions
   bound to the vanished source IP remain alive until long OS timeouts
   expire, stalling traffic failover.
3. Custom configuration must stay bidirectionally compatible with
   official Mihomo releases so users can switch kernels without editing
   config.yaml.

Solution:
- Add DefaultInterfacePriority []string to config.RawTun and
  listener/config.Tun (including slices.Equal comparison in Tun.Equal)
  with `yaml:"default-interface-priority,omitempty"` and
  `json:"default-interface-priority,omitempty"` tags, and wire it into
  tun.DefaultInterfaceMonitorOptions.PreferredInterfaces.
- Preserve bidirectional compatibility with official Mihomo:
  official builds parse YAML via UnmarshalRawConfig (yaml.Unmarshal
  without strict field rejection) and silently ignore the unknown key,
  while custom builds omit the field when empty via omitempty and fall
  back to upstream metric selection when unset.
- Add ResetSessions() to transport/anytls/session.Client,
  transport/anytls.Client, and adapter/outbound.AnyTLS, detaching
  active and idle sessions under locks and calling Session.Close()
  after releasing locks to prevent deadlocks.
- Track actual default-interface transitions (prevHas && prevName !=
  newName) in listener/sing_tun/server.go and invoke
  resetStaleConnectionsOnInterfaceChange() in listener/sing_tun/reset.go:
  reset pooled sessions first (so stream dieHook observes
  Session.IsClosed() and does not re-queue dead sessions), then close
  tracked connections in statistic.DefaultManager, while preserving
  proxies and connections explicitly pinned via interface-name to a
  different active interface.
- Add unit tests in config/tun_priority_test.go,
  listener/sing_tun/reset_test.go, and
  transport/anytls/session/client_reset_test.go.

